   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 821 of the laws of 1970 amending the town law relating to payment in lieu of taxes for property acquired for park or recreational purposes by the town of Hempstead, in relation to the term of effectiveness of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S7840",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7840-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 821 of 1970",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7840\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 821 of the laws of 1970\namending the town law relating to payment in lieu of taxes for\nproperty acquired for park or recreational purposes by the town of\nHempstead, in relation to the term of effectiveness of such chapter\n\n PURPOSE : To extend until June 30, 2010 the authorization of the Town\nof Hempstead to make payments in lieu of taxes on certain parklands in\nLido Beach - Point Lookout area.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS : Section 3 of chapter 821 of the laws of 1970\namending the Town Law is amended as it pertains to the payment. in\nlieu of taxes by the Town of Hempstead to certain districts in the\nLido Beach area by extending its termination date from June 30, 2005\nto June 30, 2010.\n\n JUSTIFICATION : The Long Beach City School District has reached its\nconstitutional tax limit so these payments have become crucial to its\nfiscal well-being. Similar bills extending this provision have been\npassed and signed into law on seven prior occasions (1975-1980,\n1980-1985, 1985-1990, 1990-1995, 1995-2000, 2000-2005, 2005-2010).\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :  Chapter 99 of the Laws of 2000.\nChapter 120 of the Laws of 2005.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : None to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE : This act shall take effect immediately/\n",
